UID:20261103-Generalelection@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:General election
DESCRIPTION:Governor: Kathy Hochul (Democratic and Working Families lines
 ) against Bruce Blakeman (Republican and Conservative lines)\, plus Cong
 ress\, the state Legislature and five charter amendments. No mayoral rac
 e this year.\n\nhttps://www.elections.ny.gov/
URL:https://www.elections.ny.gov/
CATEGORIES:democracy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20261103-Fivecharteramendmentsontheballot@nyc-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261114T015449Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Five charter amendments on the ballot
DESCRIPTION:Mamdani's Commission on Government Efficiency adopted its fin
 al report and five ballot proposals on July 23\, after 10 public hearing
 s that drew 1\,220 New Yorkers\, 264 live testimonies and 603 written su
 bmissions. Prop 1 merges the sidewalk and roadway dining approvals into 
 one application\, cutting an eight-month process to two. Prop 2 simplifi
 es procurement for small businesses and nonprofits. Prop 3 lets the Depa
 rtment of Transportation fast-track street safety work including bike la
 nes\, and speeds the sale or lease of small city properties. Prop 4 crea
 tes one permitting hub for 40 approvals now spread across 18 offices. Pr
 op 5 sets a rainy day fund target of 12% of total tax revenues and requi
 res a deposit formula. After the election the commission becomes a stand
 ing advisory board.\n\nhttps://www.nyc.gov/mayors-office/news/2026/07/co
 ge-releases-5-ballot-proposals-and-final-report-to-make-govern
URL:https://www.nyc.gov/mayors-office/news/2026/07/coge-releases-5-ballot
 -proposals-and-final-report-to-make-govern
CATEGORIES:cityhall
END:VEVENT
